-- V30: respect the old STRUCT data's HDN ("hidden") wall flag, dropped
-- entirely by the V27 conversion — flagged live: "le jardin et la
-- discothèque ne devraient pas avoir de mur à droite et en bas".
--
-- The old game's <W> element carries an HDN="1" attribute this engine
-- already has first-class support for (Wall.hidden / WallView — a hidden
-- wall still collides, just isn't drawn; see game-core/src/index.ts's own
-- demo comment, which is literally this exact Jardin STRUCT data used as
-- the documented HDN example). The conversion script never read that
-- attribute at all, so every wall came through solid regardless of source.
--
-- Model data, now respected:
--   - model_jardin: all 6 walls HDN="1" — a fully open garden, no visible
--     wall on any side (not just right/bottom).
--   - model_disco: the 2 front/entrance walls are NOT hidden, the other 2
--     (right, bottom) are HDN="1".
--   - model_maisonh / model_quizz: no HDN on any wall — unaffected.
--
-- No rescale change from V29 — same per-room factors, this migration only
-- adds "hidden": true to the walls the source data marks HDN, everything
-- else byte-identical. Verified live: Jardin's walls are gone on every
-- side, Discotchat's right/bottom walls are gone, both still walkable
-- (collision unaffected, hidden walls still block movement by design).

-- ── Jardinherbe : seul asset de texture (sol) récupéré pour ces 4 salles ────
INSERT INTO items (name, item_type, sub_type, possessable, display_image, sprite_path, sprite_key)
SELECT 'Jardinherbe', 'FURNITURE', 'FLOOR', false,
       'http://localhost:3001/textures/floors/jardinherbe.png', 'jardinherbe.png', 'floors'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM items WHERE sprite_key = 'floors' AND sprite_path = 'jardinherbe.png');


